CORE libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ none before the throw: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ none in the handler: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ count after: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
std::uncaught_exception and std::uncaught_exceptions had no body, so
their results were nondeterministic.  They now read the in-flight
exception of the exception lowering.
